            <ArticleTitle>Multiple perforation of small-intestine diverticula in a patient with Ehlers-Danlos syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>83</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.17235/reed.2016.4452/2016</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ehlers-Danlos syndrome represents a group of hereditary connective tissue disorders characterized by ligamentous hyperlaxity, fragile skin and joint hypermobility. Gastrointestinal complications in this syndrome are less well known.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
